Package: SafeShiny
Type: Package
Title: Safe Observers, Reactives and Renderers for Shiny with Execution-Time Tracking
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: c(person("Venelin", "Mitov", email = "vmitov@gmail.com",
                    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")))
Maintainer: Venelin Mitov <vmitov@gmail.com>
Description: An uncaught error inside a plain shiny::observe()/observeEvent() terminates the
  whole Shiny session, unlike an error inside a reactive() consumed only by a render output or a
  shiny::downloadHandler(), either of which Shiny already degrades gracefully on its own (a
  localized error display, or an HTTP 500 for that one download). SafeShiny provides two kinds of
  wrapper accordingly. SafeObserve()/SafeObserveEvent() are drop-in replacements for
  shiny::observe()/observeEvent() that catch and swallow errors instead of letting them crash the
  session, since nothing else would contain them. SafeRender()/SafeRenderPlot()/SafeRenderUI()/
  SafeRenderTable()/SafeDownloadHandler() instead catch, fire an onError() hook, and re-raise the
  original error unchanged, since Shiny's own native degradation already happens either way - the
  hook exists purely to give the application observability into an error Shiny is already
  silently containing. All re-raise shiny::req()/shiny::validate()'s intentional silent-stop
  conditions unchanged and never treat them as errors. Most also support optional execution-time
  tracking, to separate time spent in application business logic from time spent in Shiny's own
  reactive-graph maintenance.
